//! Rust port of the cine-rec-engine INGEST lane — wave C, the
//! DB-free core. The Python package stays the source of truth
//! (rust-port plan); every ported piece is proven against fixtures
//! generated by running the REAL Python modules.
//!
//! Landed so far in this wave:
//! * [`rate`] — `ingest/rate.py`: the pure [`rate::TokenBucket`]
//!   policy (bit-exact golden trace from the real `RateLimiter` with
//!   a monkeypatched clock/sleep) plus the async
//!   [`rate::RateLimiter`] wrapper whose lock is held across the
//!   sleep, like `asyncio.Lock` in the original.
//! * [`exports`] — `ingest/exports.py` pure core: URL builders
//!   (byte-compatible), the strict [`exports::parse_export`], the
//!   lenient [`exports::parse_line`] (KeyError/ValueError swallowed,
//!   TypeError loud — the Python `except` exactly), the streaming
//!   [`exports::LineBuffer`] with its faithful
//!   unterminated-tail-is-dropped quirk, and the
//!   [`exports::entry_passes`] starter filters. Parity fixtures were
//!   produced by the real module, streams included (a duck-typed mock
//!   session drove `iter_export_ids` end-to-end).
//! * [`pyval`] — Python conversion semantics over JSON (`int()`,
//!   `float()`, truthiness, `repr`) that the export field
//!   expressions depend on; [`date`] — the slice of `datetime.date`
//!   the URL builders need.
//!
//! The table-name-mapping lane follows in the next commit, with its
//! own parity fixtures.

pub mod date;
pub mod exports;
pub mod pyval;
pub mod rate;
